# etcd Secret encryption-at-rest key (apiserver EncryptionConfiguration).
#
# This .example is a PLACEHOLDER. The real key is the AES key the kube-apiserver
# uses to encrypt Kubernetes Secret objects before persisting them to etcd. It
# MUST NEVER be committed — custody is this offline USB-KEYS stick (or Vault).
#
# Generate a 32-byte base64 key and drop it next to this file as
#   kubernetes/encryption-key   (gitignored)
# e.g.:
#   head -c 32 /dev/urandom | base64 -w0 > kubernetes/encryption-key
#
# IMPORTANT for HA: put the SAME key file on EVERY control-plane node's KEYS
# stick. All apiservers share one etcd, so they must share one key or an
# additional control plane cannot decrypt Secrets the first one wrote.
#
# keys-provision (ensure_encryption_config) reads this before `kubeadm init`/
# `join` and writes /etc/kubernetes/encryption-config.yaml (aescbc provider). If
# absent, a fresh key is minted on the first control plane and saved to
# /etc/snapdragon/etcd-encryption.key with a WARNING to copy it to the other CPs.
# See docs/ENCRYPTION-AT-REST.md (KMS-via-Vault-Transit is the documented upgrade).
